    "advancement": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>18th-level Study of Destruction feature</em></p><p>You can conjure a meteor from the Twisting Nether as an action, causing it to appear in the air and crash down to a point you designate within 60 feet.</p><p>Creatures in a 30 feet radius of that point take [[/damage 2d8 bludgeoning]] damage and [[/damage 2d6 fire]] damage and the ground becomes difficult terrain. You can then choose to either detonate the stone, dealing [[/damage 13d10 fire]] damage to all creatures within 30 feet of the point (Dexterity save for half damage), or you can animate it as an @UUID[Compendium.wc5e-foundryvtt.summons.Actor.nw39uK5COCfP60vL]{infernal}.</p><p>The infernal rises from the crater at the end of your turn, following your commands (no action). It remains animated for 1 minute, or until killed or dismissed as a bonus action. When you dismiss the infernal, you can choose whether to merely dismiss it or force it to use its Death Burst ability.</p><p>Once you have used this ability, you cannot do so again until you finish a long rest.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
